Fix RTSP stream_source() auth for XM/iCSee cameras whose password contains
characters that need percent-encoding (e.g. !, @, #).

Upstream (icsee-ptz 5.1.6) does `quote(device.password, safe="")`. The camera
parses the RTSP URL path verbatim and does NOT percent-decode it, so the quoted
password no longer matches and the camera answers 401. Verified on hardware:
`password=X!` -> 200 OK, `password=X%21` -> 401. The live feed does not play
until the quoting is removed.

Apply to the live integration (the container and the host have `git`, not
`patch`), then restart Home Assistant:

    git -C /home/orangepi/docker-data/homeassistant/custom_components/icsee_ptz \
        apply -p1 /home/orangepi/Github/orangepi5/docker/homeassistant/icsee-ptz-rtsp-password.patch
    docker restart homeassistant

--- a/camera.py
+++ b/camera.py
@@ -100,7 +100,10 @@
     async def stream_source(self) -> str | None:
         device = self.device
         user = quote(device.username, safe="")
-        password = quote(device.password, safe="")
+        # XM parses this RTSP path verbatim and does NOT percent-decode it, so
+        # escaping the password makes it wrong and the camera replies 401.
+        # Verified on hardware: password=X! -> 200 OK, password=X%21 -> 401.
+        password = device.password
         rtsp = _rtsp(self.coordinator)
         if rtsp is None:
             # Camera without an RTSP config: only an external go2rtc can play this
